# Normalise line endings across the team.
#
# Without this, the same file differs between a Windows checkout and a
# macOS/Linux one purely by CRLF vs LF. Git then reports changes that are not
# real: `git diff` shows whole files as modified, and comparing a working tree
# against a branch flags files whose content is identical.
#
# Text files are stored in the repository with LF and checked out with the
# platform's native endings. Every blob here is already LF, so this changes no
# file content — it only makes the behaviour explicit and identical for
# everyone, instead of depending on each machine's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto

# Always LF regardless of platform: tooling that reads these expects it.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf

# Binary — never transform, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
